        "content": "\n**Gap — `requireReviewer` throw path is the security-critical branch and is completely untested:**\n```ts\n// lib/server/auth.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\n\nconst authMock = vi.fn();\nconst currentUserMock = vi.fn();\nvi.mock(\"@clerk/nextjs/server\", () => ({ auth: authMock, currentUser: currentUserMock }));\n\nimport { requireReviewer, getReviewer } from \"./auth\";\n\ndescribe(\"requireReviewer\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => { authMock.mockReset(); currentUserMock.mockReset(); });\n\n  it(\"throws when isAuthenticated is false\", async () => {\n    authMock.mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false, userId: null });\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow(/No authenticated reviewer/);\n  });\n  it(\"throws when isAuthenticated is true but userId is missing (edge desync)\", async () => {\n    authMock.mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: null });\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow();\n  });\n  it(\"returns userId and label derived via reviewerLabel\", async () => {\n    authMock.mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"u1\" });\n    currentUserMock.mockResolvedValue({ username: \"j.rao\", primaryEmailAddress: null });\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).resolves.toEqual({ userId: \"u1\", label: \"j.rao\" });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getReviewer\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null when not authenticated (does not throw)\", async () => {\n    authMock.mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false });\n    await expect(getReviewer()).resolves.toBeNull();\n  });\n  it(\"delegates to requireReviewer when authenticated\", async () => {\n    authMock.mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"u1\" });\n    currentUserMock.mockResolvedValue({ username: null, primaryEmailAddress: null });\n    await expect(getReviewer()).resolves.toEqual({ userId: \"u1\", label: \"u1\" });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**Gap — `getDb()` lazy-connect + missing-env-var failure path:**\n```ts\n// lib/db/index.test.ts\ndescribe(\"getDb\", () => {\n  it(\"throws an actionable error when DATABASE_URL is unset\", () => {\n    delete process.env.DATABASE_URL;\n    expect(() => getDb()).toThrow(/DATABASE_URL is not set/);\n  });\n  it(\"caches the connection on globalThis across calls (HMR safety)\", () => {\n    process.env.DATABASE_URL = \"postgres://x\";\n    const a = getDb();\n    const b = getDb();\n    expect(a).toBe(b);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**Gap — `listSources` row→schema parse failure is silent-crash territory:**\n```ts\n// lib/server/sources.test.ts (add)\nit(\"throws if a row from the db fails sourceSchema.parse (schema drift)\", async () => {\n  // mock getDb().select().from().orderBy() to resolve a row missing a required field\n  // assert listSources() rejects rather than returning malformed data\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "4. Route matcher (`proxy.ts`) — untested authorization boundary",
        "content": "\nThis is the single access-control gate for the whole app; a regex or matcher mistake here is a full auth bypass, and it's currently unverified.\n\n```ts\n// proxy.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { createRouteMatcher } from \"@clerk/nextjs/server\";\n\n// Test the matcher logic directly, not the exported middleware (which needs a Clerk request context)\nconst isPublicRoute = createRouteMatcher([\"/\", \"/sign-in(.*)\", \"/sign-up(.*)\"]);\n\ndescribe(\"isPublicRoute\", () => {\n  it.each([\"/\", \"/sign-in\", \"/sign-in/factor-one\", \"/sign-up\"])(\"treats %s as public\", (path) => {\n    expect(isPublicRoute(new Request(`http://x${path}`))).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it.each([\"/sources\", \"/api/sources\", \"/get-started\", \"/sign-in-fake\"])(\"treats %s as protected\", (path) => {\n    // \"/sign-in-fake\" specifically checks the (.*) suffix doesn't over-match a sibling path\n    expect(isPublicRoute(new Request(`http://x${path}`))).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\nNote: `/sign-in-fake` starting with `/sign-in` is worth explicitly checking — `createRouteMatcher`'s pattern semantics should anchor this correctly, but it's exactly the kind of thing that regresses silently.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "5. Component tests (React Testing Library) — currently 0 of ~20 components covered",
        "content": "\nTwo components have branch logic worth locking in beyond snapshot rendering:\n\n**Gap — `SourceTable` empty state and multi-object join:**\n```tsx\n// components/sources/source-table.test.tsx\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { SourceTable } from \"./source-table\";\n\ndescribe(\"SourceTable\", () => {\n  it(\"renders one row per source with kind label and side resolved\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[mockSource({ kind: \"salesforce\" })]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Salesforce\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"crm\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n  it(\"joins multiple config.objects with a comma\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[mockSource({ config: { objects: [\"Account\", \"Contact\"] } })]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Account, Contact\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n  it(\"renders an empty tbody with zero sources (no crash)\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[]} />);\n    expect(screen.queryAllByRole(\"row\")).toHaveLength(1); // header only\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**Gap — `SeverityMark` never renders the mark without its label (an explicit AGENTS.md constraint) — untested:**\n```tsx\n// components/severity-mark.test.tsx\ndescribe(\"SeverityMark\", () => {\n  it.each([1, 2, 3, 4] as const)(\"severity %d always renders its text label alongside the glyph\", (severity) => {\n    render(<SeverityMark severity={severity} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(SEVERITY_LABEL[severity])).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Summary of gaps by category",
        "content": "| Category | Gap count | Priority |\n|---|---|---|\n| No test framework configured at all | — | **Blocker** — set up Vitest first |\n| Pure function unit tests (`reviewerLabel`, `ruleSpecificity`, `cn`) | 3 functions, 0 tests | High — cheap, no mocking |\n| Zod schema boundary/refine tests | 7 schemas, 0 tests | High — these are cross-service contracts |\n| Auth error-path tests (`requireReviewer` throw, `getDb` missing env) | 2 functions, 0 tests | **Critical** — security and startup-failure paths |\n| Route-matcher / authorization boundary (`proxy.ts`) | 0 tests | **Critical** — sole access-control gate |\n| DB-backed integration tests (`listSources`, `countSourcesBySide`) | 0 tests | Medium — needs mock or test DB |\n| Component branch/edge-case tests | 0 of ~20 components | Medium |\n| True integration tests (API routes — none exist yet under `app/api`) | N/A | Note: no route handlers exist yet in this repo; add contract tests when they land, validating against `reviewActionSchema`/`createRunSchema` etc. |\n\nBiggest single risk: **`requireReviewer`'s throw branch and `proxy.ts`'s matcher are both auth-critical and both have zero coverage** — I'd start there before the pure-function tests, even though the pure functions are cheaper to write.",
